==Post-match==
[[File:José Mourinho.jpg|right|thumb|upright|alt=José Mourinho|José Mourinho (pictured) replaced Louis van Gaal as Manchester United manager days after the final.]]
Rooney was named [[Player of the match|man of the match]] and expressed admiration for his opponents: "It was a great advert for the Premier League. Credit to Palace, they’ve had a tough end to the season".<ref name=bbc3>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/36163462?page=3 | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | access-date = 13 May 2021 | title = Mourinho latest & FA Cup final reaction (3 of 28) | first = Tom | last = Rostance | date = 21 May 2016 | archive-date = 13 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210513203727/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/36163462/page/3 | url-status = live }}</ref><ref name="Finalmatchreport">{{cite news |first=Phil |last=McNulty |authorlink=Phil McNulty |title=Crystal Palace 1–2 Manchester United (aet) |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/36292265 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=21 May 2016 |access-date=22 May 2016 |archive-date=21 March 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190321112510/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/36292265 |url-status=live }}</ref>  His manager van Gaal reflected on the significance for Manchester United and his own success, saying "It is fantastic to win this title for the club, for the fans, and also for me because I now have won the cup in four countries, and not many managers have done that."<ref name=bbc3/>  Crystal Palace defender Delaney was gracious in defeat, suggesting Manchester United had deserved their victory: "They were the better side on the day, we didn't do ourselves justice. Fair play to them, no hard feelings from my part."<ref name=bbc2>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/36163462?page=2 | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | access-date = 13 May 2021 | title = Mourinho latest & FA Cup final reaction (2 of 28) | first = Tom | last = Rostance | date = 21 May 2016 | archive-date = 13 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210513203756/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/36163462/page/2 | url-status = live }}</ref>  Pardew was less magnanimous, highlighting the officiating that had gone against his side: "My players gave everything. Everything. And they deserved to win but the game is like that. We had a couple of decisions that went against us, big time. Connor was through, Wilfried had a penalty but I'm not going to bleat."<ref name=bbc2/>

Former Arsenal player [[Martin Keown]] described Clattenburg's decision not to play the advantage for Wickham's first-half opportunity as "a shocking decision" and "a massive let off for Manchester United".<ref name=bbc13>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/36163462?page=13 | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | access-date = 12 May 2021 | title = Mourinho latest & FA Cup final reaction (13 of 28) | first = Tom | last = Rostance | date = 21 May 2016 | archive-date = 13 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210513203808/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/36163462/page/13 | url-status = live }}</ref>  Alan Smith, writing in ''The Guardian'', described the decision as "baffling" and "dismal".<ref name=guardasit3/>  Clattenburg was later criticised by former players, including [[Alan Shearer]] and [[Rio Ferdinand]], for some of the decisions he made during the match against Crystal Palace.<ref name=ie/>  He went on to officiate the [[2016 UEFA Champions League Final]] and was named the Best Referee of the Year at the Globe Soccer Awards in December 2016.<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.premierleague.com/news/257598 | publisher = [[Premier League]] | title = Clattenburg named world's best referee | date = 28 December 2016 | access-date = 11 May 2021 | archive-date = 23 November 2020 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20201123225929/https://www.premierleague.com/news/257598 | url-status = live }}</ref>  The following year, in an interview with the ''[[Irish Examiner]]'', Clattenburg admitted that he "made a couple of errors" during the FA Cup match and that he believed he "could have done better".<ref name=ie>{{Cite web | url = https://www.irishexaminer.com/sport/soccer/arid-20437360.html | work = [[Irish Examiner]] | title = 'If I make a mistake, it beats me up' – The trials and tribulations of Premier League referee Mark Clattenburg | date = 2 January 2017 | access-date = 11 May 2021 | first = Rob | last = Harris | archive-date = 14 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210514124338/https://www.irishexaminer.com/sport/soccer/arid-20437360.html | url-status = live }}</ref>

As winners, Manchester United qualified for the [[2016 FA Community Shield]] and the group stage of the [[2016–17 UEFA Europa League]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaleague/season=2017/accesslist/index.html |title=2016/17 UEFA Europa League access list |publisher=[[UEFA]] |access-date=24 April 2016 |archive-date=19 April 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160419160804/http://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaleague/season=2017/accesslist/index.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> Since they had also qualified for the Europa League group stage based on their league position, Southampton entered the group stage (taking the league spot from Manchester United instead of their original spot in the third qualifying round), while Southampton's spot in the third qualifying round was given to West Ham United as the highest placed Premier League team not already qualified for European competitions.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.uefa.org/about-uefa/executive-committee/news/newsid=1999120.html |title=Strategic talks in Dubrovnik |publisher=[[UEFA]] |access-date=24 April 2016 | date = 20 September 2013| archive-date=20 September 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150920032254/http://www.uefa.org/about-uefa/executive-committee/news/newsid=1999120.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

Five days after the final, van Gaal was dismissed by Manchester United with his replacement [[José Mourinho]] being appointed the following day.<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/36356584 | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | access-date = 12 May 2021 | date = 26 May 2016 | title = Louis van Gaal: Manchester United sack manager | first1 = Simon | last1 = Stone | first2 = Dan | last2 = Roan | archive-date = 26 March 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210326203052/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/36356584 | url-status = live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web| url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/36363365| title = Jose Mourinho: Man Utd confirm former Chelsea boss as new manager| date = 27 May 2016| publisher = [[BBC Sport]]| access-date = 12 May 2021| archive-date = 1 April 2018| archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20180401080746/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/36363365| url-status = live}}</ref> In the following season, United were unable to defend their trophy as they were eliminated in the quarter-finals, after a 1–0 defeat to Chelsea at [[Stamford Bridge (stadium)|Stamford Bridge]].<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/39176050 | title = Chelsea 1–0 Manchester United | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | access-date = 13 May 2021 | date = 13 March 2017 | first = Phil | last = McNulty | authorlink = Phil McNulty | archive-date = 6 January 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075246/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/39176050 | url-status = live }}</ref>  Pardew was dismissed in December 2016 with Crystal Palace one point above the [[Promotion and relegation|relegation]] positions in the Premier League, and was replaced by [[Sam Allardyce]] the following day.<ref>{{Cite web| url =https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/38408138| title =Alan Pardew: Crystal Palace sack manager with club 17th in Premier League| publisher =[[BBC Sport]]| access-date =13 May 2021| date =22 December 2016| archive-date =8 November 2020| archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20201108162402/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/38408138| url-status =live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news| url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/38419024| title = Sam Allardyce appointed Crystal Palace manager as Alan Pardew's successor| first = David| last = Ornstein| work = BBC Sport| access-date = 13 May 2021| date = 23 December 2016| archive-date = 8 November 2020| archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20201108144539/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/38419024| url-status = live}}</ref>  Crystal Palace were knocked out in the fourth round, losing 3–0 at home against [[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] the following month.<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/38700695 | title = Crystal Palace 0–3 Manchester City | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | access-date = 13 May 2021 | date = 28 January 2017 | archive-date = 30 October 2020 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20201030020605/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/38700695 | url-status = live }}</ref>

